{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfnxsejDf7Wuzv3Pme2SJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, now I understand the structure. I need to:\n1. Add a `shipping_cost` function to `app/pricing.py`\n2. Use `Decimal` for all money amounts\n3. Follow the type hints pattern\n4. Use the logger\n5. The logic:\n   - Get the subtotal using the existing `subtotal(order)` function\n   - If express: base is $10.00, else base is $0 if subtotal >= $50 else $5.99\n   - Return as Decimal\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef shipping_cost(order: Order, express: bool = False) -> Decimal:\n    order_subtotal = subtotal(order)\n    free_shipping_threshold = Decimal(\"50.00\")\n    standard_shipping = Decimal(\"5.99\")\n    express_surcharge = Decimal(\"10.00\")\n    \n    if express:\n        if order_subtotal >= free_shipping_threshold:\n            cost = express_surcharge\n        else:\n            cost = standard_shipping + express_surcharge\n    else:\n        if order_subtotal >= free_shipping_threshold:\n            cost = Decimal(\"0.00\")\n        else:\n            cost = standard_shipping\n    \n    return to_cents(cost)\n```\n\nActually, let me think about this more carefully. The requirements are:\n- Orders with subtotal >= $50.00: ship free (standard shipping is $0)\n- Orders with subtotal < $50.00: standard shipping is $5.99\n- Express shipping adds $10.00 on top, always\n\nSo:\n- Standard (express=False): if subtotal >= $50 then $0, else $5.99\n- Express (express=True): add $10 to the above\n\nLet me refactor:\n\n```python\ndef shipping_cost(order: Order, express: bool = False) -> Decimal:\n    order_subtotal = subtotal(order)\n    free_shipping_threshold = Decimal(\"50.00\")\n    standard_shipping = Decimal(\"5.99\")\n    express_surcharge = Decimal(\"10.00\")\n    \n    if order_subtotal >= free_shipping_threshold:\n        cost = Decimal(\"0.00\")\n    else:\n        cost = standard_shipping\n    \n    if express:\n        cost += express_surcharge\n    \n    return to_cents(cost)\n```\n\nThis version is simpler and avoids duplicating the threshold check. I'll add a log statement and integrate this into the file next.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8061,"cache_read_input_tokens":20822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8061},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"tools_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":26832}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f7fdb41-d2fa-48be-a602-fec36d4bebad","uuid":"005bd194-a307-4f02-a101-9013269be717","request_id":"req_011CfnxseVqCCRWnj5mTgLqA"}
